{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"c86d0636e0edcf3d","name":"card_unit_beriev_be_4","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_beriev_be_4","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BERIEV BE-4","text":"Your units cost 2 less to deploy. When you deploy a unit, Retreat this unit.","flavorText":"The Beriev Be-4, originally designated KOR-2, was a Soviet flying boat that was developed and used during World War II. It was primarily designed for maritime reconnaissance and bombing missions. The Be-4 was a twin-engine aircraft featuring a biplane configuration with a large central float and smaller stabilizing floats attached to the wings. One of the notable characteristics of the Be-4 was its ability to operate from both land and water. It had a crew of three and was equipped with defensive armament, including machine guns, and it was well-suited for a variety of missions, including coastal patrols, anti-submarine warfare, and reconnaissance over maritime areas. A total of 47 aircraft were produced and they were in service throughout the war, mainly in the Black Sea, Baltic Sea, and Arctic Ocean regions.","faction":"Soviet","type":"fighter","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_beriev_be_4","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_beriev_be_4_title","SourceString":"BERIEV BE-4","LocalizedString":"BERIEV BE-4"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":1,"defense":4,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_beriev_be_4_text","SourceString":"Your units cost 2 less to deploy. When you deploy a unit, Retreat this unit.","LocalizedString":"Your units cost 2 less to deploy. When you deploy a unit, Retreat this unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_beriev_be_4_history","SourceString":"The Beriev Be-4, originally designated KOR-2, was a Soviet flying boa